# Radiology Patient Flow

Radiology owns imaging execution for encounter-linked orders; keep the workbench focused on scheduling, performing studies, capturing assets, and finalizing reports.

## Stage Sequence

- Order received from OPD, IPD, ICU, or clinical dialog.
- Billing gate checked when required.
- Modality, room, and equipment assigned.
- Study started and assets captured.
- Report drafted, finalized, and attested.
- Addendum issued only when needed.

## Handoffs

- Doctor or clinical user owns order placement.
- Radiology clerk owns scheduling and assignment.
- Radiographer owns study execution and asset upload.
- Radiologist owns report draft, finalization, and addendum.
- OPD or IPD orchestrators own stage progression after the report returns.

## Hard Invariants

- Must not create encounters or advance patient stages directly.
- Must not own equipment maintenance or biomedical workflows.
- Must keep every study linked to the source encounter.
- Must not blur outpatient and inpatient queue contexts.

## Allowed Critical Actions

- Use the radiology workbench route as the canonical imaging workspace.
- May support pay-now or bill-later at order time when policy requires it.
- Keep PACS sync and report release visible when configured.
- Surface completed studies back to the receiving clinician timeline.

